# Build Artifacts

/tags
/.build/
/build*
# /build* is meant for build DIRECTORIES, but the prefix glob also swallows the build
# SCRIPTS beside them -- build_vulkan.bat was untrackable for that reason alone, while the
# sibling tree portable/ik_llama tracks its own copy. Negate rather than loosen the rule:
# widening /build* to /build*/ would stop ignoring anything else literally named build*.
# Ported 2026-08-31 from portable/ik_llama_merged/.gitignore, which had the GENERAL rule while
# this canonical tree had only the three per-file negations above. Naming each recipe means every
# new one is invisible until someone notices -- and the merged tree's own comment records what
# that cost: `!build_*.bat` alone still left _build_gemma4_kv_fix_incremental.bat hidden, "which
# is how it kept 5 dead-root refs after the other seven were fixed".
# This is a fix that existed ONLY in a tree measured as droppable (124 commits, 0 unique). Found
# while auditing what would be lost before deleting it. A build artifact is never a .bat.
!/build_vulkan.bat
!/build_sm120*.bat
!/build_ninja*.bat
!build_*.bat
# ...and the underscore-prefixed ones, which are the names actually used here.
!_build_*.bat
/release
/debug
/libllama.so
/llama-*
/vulkan-shaders-gen
/rpc-server
/out/
/tmp/
/autogen-*.md
/common/build-info.cpp

